\mt1 THE GOSPEL ACCORDING TO ST. MARK  
\c 16  
\p
\v 1 \w And\w* when the \w sabbath\w* was \w past\w*, \w Mary\w* \w Magdalene\w*, \w and\w* \w Mary\w* \w the\w* \add mother\add* of \w James\w*, \w and\w* \w Salome\w*, had \w bought\w* sweet \w spices\w*, \w that\w* they might \w come\w* and \w anoint\w* \w him\w*.  
\v 2 \w And\w* \w very\w* early in the \w morning\w* the \w first\w* \add day\add* of the \w week\w*, they \w came\w* \w unto\w* the \w sepulchre\w* at the \w rising\w* of the \w sun\w*.  
\v 3 \w And\w* they \w said\w* \w among\w* \w themselves\w*, \w Who\w* shall \w roll\w* \w us\w* \w away\w* the \w stone\w* \w from\w* the \w door\w* of the \w sepulchre\w*?  
\v 4 \w And\w* when they \w looked\w*, they \w saw\w* \w that\w* the \w stone\w* was rolled \w away\w*: \w for\w* it \w was\w* \w very\w* \w great\w*.  
\v 5 \w And\w* \w entering\w* \w into\w* the \w sepulchre\w*, they \w saw\w* a young \w man\w* \w sitting\w* \w on\w* the right \w side\w*, \w clothed\w* in a \w long\w* \w white\w* \w garment\w*; \w and\w* they were \w affrighted\w*.  
\v 6 \w And\w* he \w saith\w* unto \w them\w*, \w Be\w* \w not\w* \w affrighted\w*: Ye \w seek\w* \w Jesus\w* of \w Nazareth\w*, \w which\w* was \w crucified\w*: he is \w risen\w*; he \w is\w* \w not\w* \w here\w*: \w behold\w* the \w place\w* \w where\w* they \w laid\w* \w him\w*.  
\v 7 \w But\w* go your \w way\w*, \w tell\w* \w his\w* \w disciples\w* \w and\w* \w Peter\w* \w that\w* he goeth \w before\w* \w you\w* \w into\w* \w Galilee\w*: \w there\w* shall ye \w see\w* \w him\w*, \w as\w* he \w said\w* unto \w you\w*.  
\v 8 \w And\w* they went \w out\w* \w quickly\w*, and \w fled\w* \w from\w* the \w sepulchre\w*; \w for\w* \w they\w* \w trembled\w* \w and\w* were \w amazed\w*: \w neither\w* said \w they\w* any \w thing\w* to \w any\w* \add man\add*; \w for\w* they were \w afraid\w*.   
\p
\v 9 ¶ Now \w when\w* \add Jesus\add* was \w risen\w* \w early\w* the \w first\w* \add day\add* of the \w week\w*, he \w appeared\w* \w first\w* to \w Mary\w* \w Magdalene\w*, out \w of\w* \w whom\w* he had \w cast\w* \w seven\w* \w devils\w*.  
\v 10 \add And\add* she \w went\w* and \w told\w* them \w that\w* had \w been\w* \w with\w* \w him\w*, as they \w mourned\w* \w and\w* \w wept\w*.  
\v 11 And \w they\w*, when they had \w heard\w* \w that\w* he was \w alive\w*, \w and\w* had been \w seen\w* \w of\w* \w her\w*, believed \w not\w*.   
\p
\v 12 ¶ \w After\w* \w that\w* he \w appeared\w* \w in\w* \w another\w* \w form\w* unto \w two\w* \w of\w* \w them\w*, as they \w walked\w*, and \w went\w* \w into\w* the \w country\w*.  
\v 13 And \w they\w* \w went\w* and \w told\w* \add it\add* unto the \w residue\w*: \w neither\w* believed \w they\w* \w them\w*.   
\p
\v 14 ¶ \w Afterward\w* he \w appeared\w* unto the \w eleven\w* as \w they\w* sat at \w meat\w*, \w and\w* \w upbraided\w* them with \w their\w* \w unbelief\w* \w and\w* hardness of \w heart\w*, \w because\w* they \w believed\w* \w not\w* them \w which\w* had \w seen\w* \w him\w* after he was \w risen\w*.  
\v 15 \w And\w* he \w said\w* unto \w them\w*, \wj  \+w Go ye\+w* \+w into\+w* \+w all\+w* \+w the world\+w*, \+w and preach\+w* \+w the gospel\+w* \+w to every\+w* \+w creature\+w*.\wj*  
\v 16 \wj  \+w He\+w* \+w that believeth\+w* \+w and\+w* \+w is baptized\+w* \+w shall be saved\+w*; \+w but\+w* \+w he\+w* \+w that believeth not\+w* \+w shall be damned\+w*.\wj*  
\v 17 \wj  \+w And\+w* \+w these\+w* \+w signs\+w* \+w shall follow\+w* \+w them\+w* \+w that believe\+w*; \+w In\+w* \+w my\+w* \+w name\+w* \+w shall they cast out\+w* \+w devils\+w*; \+w they shall speak\+w* \+w with new\+w* \+w tongues\+w*;\wj*  
\v 18 \wj  \+w They shall take up\+w* \+w serpents\+w*; \+w and if\+w* \+w they drink\+w* \+w any\+w* \+w deadly thing\+w*, \+w it shall\+w* \+w not\+w* \+w hurt\+w* \+w them\+w*; \+w they shall lay\+w* \+w hands\+w* \+w on\+w* \+w the sick\+w*, \+w and\+w* \+w they shall\+w* \+w recover\+w*.\wj*   
\p
\v 19 ¶ \w So\w* \w then\w* \w after\w* the \w Lord\w* had \w spoken\w* unto \w them\w*, he was received \w up\w* \w into\w* \w heaven\w*, \w and\w* \w sat\w* \w on\w* the right \w hand\w* of \w God\w*.  
\v 20 \w And\w* \w they\w* went \w forth\w*, and \w preached\w* every \w where\w*, the \w Lord\w* working \w with\w* \add them\add*, \w and\w* \w confirming\w* the \w word\w* \w with\w* \w signs\w* \w following\w*. \w Amen\w*.
